input.text:
**Code Change Description:**
The motivation is to improve the interoperability of proxied MCP tools. Previously, when a Spring AI tool callback returned a serialized list of MCP contents, it would be treated as a single `TextContent` object by the receiving system. This prevented downstream components from correctly identifying or rendering specific content types like images, audio, or resources. By allowing the system to re-parse the JSON-serialized list into typed `McpSchema.Content` objects, the implementation ensures that structured data remains accessible and correctly typed through the MCP protocol lifecycle.
Introduced a new utility method `McpToolUtils.parseContentList(String)` and integrated it into the `toSharedSyncToolSpecification` method. This change adds the capability to parse serialized strings back into structured MCP content objects (such as `TextContent`, `ImageContent`, `AudioContent`, and `ResourceLink`) when a tool callback returns a JSON-serialized list of contents. It also adds robust error handling to fall back to plain text if parsing fails, and provides comprehensive unit tests to verify the parsing of various content types.

